# --- Database (Vercel Postgres / Neon) ---
# In Vercel dashboard: Storage → Create → Postgres. The integration sets these
# automatically. For local dev, copy the "POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL" from the dashboard.
DATABASE_URL="postgres://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/DB?sslmode=require"

# --- Auth.js ---
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
AUTH_SECRET="replace-with-32-bytes-base64"
# Optional: explicitly pin the URL in production. Vercel auto-provides this.
# AUTH_URL="https://your-domain.vercel.app"

# --- Upstash Redis (rate limiting) ---
# Free tier at upstash.com, or add it via Vercel: Storage → Create → Upstash Redis.
# If unset, rate limiting degrades to a per-instance in-memory fallback (NOT
# recommended in prod — a distributed attacker can exceed limits across instances).
# The code reads either the native UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_* names below OR the
# KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN pair that Vercel's Upstash integration
# auto-provisions, so the integration works with no manual env-var aliasing.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=""
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=""
